<title>USA: Coca-Cola Co benefits from C-C Amatil.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola Co benefits from C-C Amatil.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>AX deal</p>
<p>Coca-Cola Co said Tuesday it expects a second-quarter, after-tax gain of $200 million from the sale of Coca-Cola Bottlers Philippines Inc to Coca-Cola Amatil.</p>
<p>Coca-Cola Bottlers Philippines was 70 percent owned by San Miguel Corp and 30 percent owned by Coca-Cola.</p>
<p>Coca-Cola Amatil, an Australia-based bottler that is one-third owned by Coca-Cola, acquired the Filipino bottler in a stock swap valued at A$3.4 billion.</p>
<p>Coca-Cola said the gain will be partially additive to its second quarter and full-year results.</p>
</text>
